<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-FAI sale to MMI terminated.</title>
<headline>RTRS-FAI sale to MMI terminated.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>A deal which would have seen insurer MMI Ltd buy the general insurance operations of FAI Insurances Ltd in New Zealand, Fiji and Papua New Guinea has been terminated, the companies said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>A statement to the Australian Stock Exchange said the sale had been terminated by mutual agreement because the two companies could not agree on a final sale price.</p>
<p>The proposed sale had been announced on July 7 and conditional contracts had been exchanged.</p>
<p>FAI later said the sale of its New Zealand and Pacific Island insurance operations would raise A$50 million and deliver a profit above carrying value.</p>
</text>
